+# Additional exact native Definition findings
+
+This opt-in successor retains the original registry versions and all original paused/drained initial-wave, frozen frontier, baseline, successful handoff, original Luna keep, unassigned draft Definition, full root source, literal edits and no-native-reading-coverage guards. It changes no source or original native report/output.
+
+`origin_kind:native-open-finding` now admits two explicit `finding_shape` values in addition to the unchanged original sparse shape:
+
+* `classified-definition`: the observed exact classified rich object, with fatal logic/open status, current item path, literal original source excerpt, concrete affected use/invalidated claim/minimality/reason, actual HTTPS source references and exact identical individual final output. Root correspondence and independent classification remain required and must agree with original severity.
+* `plural-report-reference`: the observed individual detailed open object without a severity, with exact canonical ledger path, open status, concrete affected_use/reason and empty source URLs. The final output is the exact four-field plural `record-open-findings` object (ledger/action/route/reason), with no fabricated ID. Its `repair_notes.report` must name the exact immutable detailed report. Separate root literal correspondence links the individual detailed finding to that actual plural summary and full current source. Root supplies classification separately; it never edits original native fields.
+
+Both use existing exact `finding`, `output_finding`, indices and root `open_finding_correspondence`; the latter report excerpt comes from actual affected-use/reason (or rich prose), and output excerpt from the actual plural reason or rich prose. Unknown shapes, extra keys, arbitrary prose, wrong action/path, invented output IDs or missing exact report reference fail. No ID is hardcoded. Work admission grants no mathematical acceptance, native finding, native source reading or current review; normal 5.2 remains owed.
+
+Actual observed provenance: unit5 report ledger_updates12–14 uses plural-report-reference for the three unassigned information Definitions; final output ledger_updates1 is a plural report reference, not per-ID evidence. Unit56 report/output ledger_updates4 supplies the rich quiver Definition object. No session journal payload was read.
